- Who makes no sense at all, ever.


00:13:00.629 --> 00:13:02.392
Why don't you have another drink, Mom.


00:13:03.933 --> 00:13:06.128
Katie, napkin me.


00:13:06.302 --> 00:13:08.793
I have got to impress Guy Morgan...


00:13:09.205 --> 00:13:12.436
...so I can stop pretending to care
about this insufferable school...


00:13:12.608 --> 00:13:16.374
...and we can all move to Hollywood where
no one pretends to care about anything.


00:13:16.545 --> 00:13:20.174
Mom, I think that you're forgetting
about the most important thing. Me.


00:13:21.116 --> 00:13:23.516
Guy will give me a deal
as soon as he hears me sing.


00:13:23.686 --> 00:13:26.280
- I doubt that.
- No, I've been practicing really hard.


00:13:26.455 --> 00:13:29.322
My voice teacher says
I've transcended to a whole new level.


00:13:29.492 --> 00:13:30.516
Yeah, I doubt it.


00:13:30.693 --> 00:13:33.253
When my first single drops,
I'll buy you that mansion...


00:13:33.429 --> 00:13:35.363
...in the Hollywood Hills...


00:13:35.531 --> 00:13:38.557
...and you can finally afford
to have your legs lengthened.


00:13:38.734 --> 00:13:40.759
- Oh, ba...
- Ms. Gail.


00:13:40.936 --> 00:13:42.904
- Miss Bev has clarity.
Katie.


00:13:43.072 --> 00:13:44.096
- You see...
- Look.


00:13:44.273 --> 00:13:48.141
- The lowly peasant tills the soil
for 40 years without any rain.


00:13:48.310 --> 00:13:51.711
But the unemployed salesman
who has recently discovered hydroponics...


00:13:51.881 --> 00:13:54.975
...all of a sudden gets disgusted by the...
- And see? No sense.


00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:57.448
- That didn't make any sense.
- Let me finish. You...


00:13:57.620 --> 00:13:59.554
Oh, I doubt it. You have me pray all day.


00:13:59.722 --> 00:14:01.952
- I don't feel nothing.
- You don't have a soul.


00:14:02.124 --> 00:14:05.321
No, you don't have soul.
- I have a many souls. I'll give you one.


00:14:05.494 --> 00:14:09.760
- Where's your third eye? Turn that thing on.
- I have a fourth eye too. You wanna see it?


00:14:09.932 --> 00:14:11.900
- What?
- Shh.


00:14:12.401 --> 00:14:15.928
I wanna be 6'4". Wow me, Bev.


00:14:18.474 --> 00:14:23.912
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:24.079 --> 00:14:26.639
Just stop. Stop the wowing, okay?


00:14:26.815 --> 00:14:28.908
What's wrong?
- Somehow you've gotten worse.


00:14:29.084 --> 00:14:30.813
I don't know how that was possible...


00:14:30.986 --> 00:14:33.614
...but there isn't enough Auto-Tune
that's gonna fix you.


00:14:33.789 --> 00:14:37.122
- Well, Katie's bad playing threw me off.
- I don't think it was that.


00:14:37.293 --> 00:14:38.920
Again.


00:14:39.094 --> 00:14:40.652
Really? Okay.


00:14:40.829 --> 00:14:46.461
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:46.635 --> 00:14:47.761
Ouch.


00:14:47.937 --> 00:14:50.997
I could belch the song better.


00:14:52.608 --> 00:14:54.769
Have you been drinking
the floor wax again?


00:14:54.944 --> 00:14:56.411
Anything to forget I live here.


00:14:56.579 --> 00:14:59.480
Ugh. My head is buzzing
like a skeeter on a septic tank.


00:14:59.648 --> 00:15:03.550
- Ravi, meditate me.
Good luck, buddy.


00:15:03.919 --> 00:15:07.582
Well, it doesn't matter,
because I have my own plan.


00:15:11.794 --> 00:15:14.160
Does it make me a bad person
that I kind of enjoyed that?


00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:16.059
No.


00:15:16.231 --> 00:15:18.529
Hmm. Nice work.


00:15:30.713 --> 00:15:34.012
- Guess who's on his way over.
- Not now, Victor, I'm busy.


00:15:34.183 --> 00:15:36.651
Guess or prepare to get creamed.


00:15:47.129 --> 00:15:50.223
Victor! Victor! Victor, stop!


00:15:55.104 --> 00:15:56.833
<i>I've got rings on my fingers</i>


00:15:57.006 --> 00:15:58.098
<i>And glitter in my hair</i>


00:15:58.273 --> 00:16:02.369
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:16:02.544 --> 00:16:03.875
<i>I'm gonna run...</i>


00:16:04.046 --> 00:16:06.810
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Victor, what are you doing?


00:16:07.249 --> 00:16:08.546
Victor!


00:16:08.717 --> 00:16:11.948
Victor, where did you put my clothes?


00:16:12.121 --> 00:16:14.282
- Surprise!
- What? No.


00:16:17.793 --> 00:16:19.420
I'm gonna kill you. Victor!


00:16:29.338 --> 00:16:30.498
Oh, hi, Katie.


00:16:30.673 --> 00:16:32.072
You are evil. Let me in.


00:16:32.241 --> 00:16:35.677
I control every lock on this property.


00:16:35.844 --> 00:16:37.505
Crap.


00:16:40.916 --> 00:16:42.611
This is insane.


00:16:42.785 --> 00:16:46.846
Yeah, try the shed, it's unlocked, idiot.


00:16:56.632 --> 00:16:58.725
You gotta be kidding me.


00:17:00.469 --> 00:17:02.096
Crap.


00:17:05.407 --> 00:17:09.002
How did such an untalented daughter
spring from my loins?


00:17:09.178 --> 00:17:12.978
Focus, Ms. Gail. We are making
an offering to your personal deity.


00:17:13.148 --> 00:17:15.275
Tell him to give me fame and fortune.


00:17:15.451 --> 00:17:17.146
Not exactly how it works.


00:17:17.319 --> 00:17:19.879
<i>Now, breathe through your Mula Bandha.</i>


00:17:20.055 --> 00:17:23.115
Oh, honey, if I could do that,
I'd get a million hits on YouTube.


00:17:23.292 --> 00:17:25.522
How much longer is this gonna take?
Ugh.


00:17:25.694 --> 00:17:27.821
The prayer or the fame and fortune?


00:17:30.165 --> 00:17:31.632
Ha, ha. See you later.


00:17:37.806 --> 00:17:39.671
Victor.


00:17:43.512 --> 00:17:44.945
Katie?


00:17:46.148 --> 00:17:48.378
- Luke.
- Katie.


00:17:48.584 --> 00:17:51.849
- Are you wearing a doormat?
- Yes.


00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:54.784
- Welcome.
- Why, thank you.


00:17:55.824 --> 00:17:57.655
The truth. Um...


00:17:58.961 --> 00:18:02.294
My stepbrother locked me
outside of the house.


00:18:02.464 --> 00:18:03.795
Naked.


00:18:04.833 --> 00:18:07.131
Oh, sorry. You should...
You should take my jacket.


00:18:07.302 --> 00:18:08.826
Oh.
- Oh, no, no.


00:18:11.273 --> 00:18:12.365
There.


00:18:12.541 --> 00:18:15.738
- Thanks. Now the pants.
- Hmm?


00:18:20.349 --> 00:18:21.976
I'm kidding.


00:18:22.518 --> 00:18:24.349
- You got me.
- Ha, ha.


00:18:24.686 --> 00:18:25.710
No, no.


00:18:25.888 --> 00:18:29.289
One more parent-teacher conference,
I swear I'm gonna lose it.


00:18:29.458 --> 00:18:31.653
Look at me. I'm an educator.


00:18:32.261 --> 00:18:36.925
I have no real skills. And I will die
before I go back to my daddy's farm.


00:18:37.432 --> 00:18:41.232
You tell my personal deity
to help me achieve Guy Morgan. Do it.


00:18:41.403 --> 00:18:43.997
I'll put another banana on the altar.


00:18:47.876 --> 00:18:49.537
What is that?


00:18:50.112 --> 00:18:52.376
Do you hear angels singing?


00:18:52.548 --> 00:18:54.516
Perhaps the gods
have answered your prayer.


00:18:55.717 --> 00:18:57.446
Hey. What...?


00:19:10.299 --> 00:19:12.790
<i>- This is Gail Van Ravensway.
Hello.</i>


00:19:12.968 --> 00:19:14.595
Guy Morgan here. How are you?


00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:16.897
Oh, well, hello, Guy.


00:19:17.072 --> 00:19:19.336
What a surprise
to see you calling this number.


00:19:19.508 --> 00:19:20.532
Do you hear this?


00:19:20.709 --> 00:19:22.370
<i>I can justify</i>


00:19:22.544 --> 00:19:24.239
That's the demo your girl, Katie...


00:19:24.413 --> 00:19:26.745
<i>... slipped into my briefcase.</i>


00:19:26.915 --> 00:19:29.110
And it sounds like money, dear.


00:19:29.284 --> 00:19:31.149
She gave you a CD?


00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:34.687
Oh, well. Well, ain't that the berries.


00:19:35.924 --> 00:19:39.792
Ravi, what frigging god did you pray to?


00:19:41.029 --> 00:19:45.125
Guy, yeah, it seems someone's
not being entirely honest here.


00:19:47.102 --> 00:19:49.297
Katie, somebody get that door!


00:19:50.439 --> 00:19:51.997
So...


00:19:52.875 --> 00:19:55.002
...that meeting today...


00:19:55.177 --> 00:19:57.975
...it was obvious
that your dad doesn't get you.


00:19:58.313 --> 00:20:00.372
He's an idiot for not liking your music.


00:20:00.549 --> 00:20:02.983
Well, it's... It's complicated.


00:20:03.252 --> 00:20:04.446
I'm gonna just, uh...


00:20:05.921 --> 00:20:07.821
Is it as complicated as me...


00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:11.118
...getting stuck outside
in only a welcome mat?


00:20:11.393 --> 00:20:15.124
That's not complicated.
That is a gift from God.


00:20:20.035 --> 00:20:22.833
Luke. Katie. What are you doing?


00:20:23.005 --> 00:20:26.065
Well, it seems your brother
is Satan's very own personal Mini-Me.


00:20:26.241 --> 00:20:28.505
Oh, I know, tell me about it. Come on in.


00:20:32.481 --> 00:20:34.142
Oh, my God, did you work out today?


00:20:35.817 --> 00:20:37.114
- Sit down.
- Ooh, look at this.


00:20:37.286 --> 00:20:40.380
- Ha, ha. Some lemonade.
- Why, thank you.


00:20:40.555 --> 00:20:43.023
You know, my stepsister,
she has body issues...


00:20:43.191 --> 00:20:45.352
...so I don't like
to discourage her nudity.


00:20:45.527 --> 00:20:46.721
That's interesting.


00:20:46.895 --> 00:20:49.659
- She's absolutely lovely...
- Would you like an appetizer?


00:20:49.831 --> 00:20:51.059
<i>Oh, fromage.</i>


00:20:51.233 --> 00:20:52.860
I only have cheese.


00:20:56.038 --> 00:20:58.006
I just got off the phone
with Guy Morgan.


00:20:58.173 --> 00:21:00.073
Your phone.


00:21:03.111 --> 00:21:05.978
He just loved that little demo
you left him.


00:21:06.148 --> 00:21:07.706
I have underestimated you.


00:21:08.283 --> 00:21:10.114
It'd make me proud
if I cared about you.


00:21:10.285 --> 00:21:13.379
- I didn't lie about anything.
- Oh, but, chicken, you did.


00:21:13.555 --> 00:21:16.183
At least that's what Guy thinks,
now that I've clarified.


00:21:16.358 --> 00:21:20.556
I told him it was Bev's demo
and that you stole it from her.


00:21:20.729 --> 00:21:23.994
- But you can't do that. That's my song.
- It's Bev's song.


00:21:24.166 --> 00:21:27.602
And Guy can't wait to see her perform it
at the Showcase.


00:21:27.769 --> 00:21:30.897
If you try to contact him, I'll deny
everything and lock you in the basement.


00:21:31.073 --> 00:21:36.204
- She can't sing to save her life.
- No, but you can, can't you?


00:21:37.479 --> 00:21:39.640
Now, let's hear this amazing voice.


00:21:45.053 --> 00:21:49.683
<i>Like a malignant tumor
She's got no sense of humor</i>


00:21:49.858 --> 00:21:53.954
<i>Just like a swollen blister
It's best to just resist her</i>


00:21:54.129 --> 00:21:57.895
<i>She's not exactly a witch
She's just a terrible bi...</i>


00:21:58.367 --> 00:22:00.028
Well, your lyrics stink.


00:22:00.202 --> 00:22:02.363
But Guy's right, you've got chops.


00:22:05.607 --> 00:22:08.303
Do you know what other instruments
I'm good at?


00:22:08.877 --> 00:22:12.335
I have a feeling I could get in trouble
with a question like that.


00:22:12.781 --> 00:22:14.749
I like trouble.


00:22:16.284 --> 00:22:17.410
Hey, kids.


00:22:18.720 --> 00:22:22.156
- Good evening, Miss Van Ravensway.
- Sorry, I need you to go. Now.


00:22:22.324 --> 00:22:25.088
Family emergency. I need Bev
to help me pass a kidney stone.


00:22:25.260 --> 00:22:29.094
- So she had a lovely evening. Ta-ta.
- Are you trying to ruin my life?


00:22:29.398 --> 00:22:34.631
I have figured out a way for you
to wow Guy Morgan in the Showcase.


00:22:34.836 --> 00:22:37.304
- So you do think I've improved?
- Oh, no, honey.


00:22:37.572 --> 00:22:40.132
But my month of spiritual devotion
has taught me...


00:22:40.308 --> 00:22:42.276
...that God works in annoying ways.


00:22:42.444 --> 00:22:45.504
How am I to wow Guy Morgan
if I supposedly can't sing?


00:22:45.680 --> 00:22:48.740
You can't, but Katie can.


00:22:48.917 --> 00:22:51.613
- What?
- I know. Like I said, annoying.


00:22:51.787 --> 00:22:55.086
We'll record her voice
and you will lip synch.


00:22:55.257 --> 00:22:57.088
What if I don't want to?


00:22:58.193 --> 00:23:01.924
Don't you get snarky with me,
you ungrateful toad.


00:23:02.097 --> 00:23:04.156
- I saved your life.
- You didn't do anything.


00:23:04.332 --> 00:23:06.596
- My dad married you.
- Yeah, and then he died.


00:23:06.768 --> 00:23:10.329
I tried to put you in foster care,
but they was all fulled up on ugly.


00:23:10.505 --> 00:23:11.995
- Funny.
- I thought it was...


00:23:12.174 --> 00:23:13.641
...because you don't wanna look bad.


00:23:15.243 --> 00:23:17.370
Katie, if you don't sing...


00:23:17.546 --> 00:23:20.674
...I'm gonna find a way for that savings
your dad left to disappear.


00:23:21.083 --> 00:23:25.281
That means, you forget college,
moving out, you're stuck here with me.


00:23:25.454 --> 00:23:29.288
But, pumpkin, we're gonna have
so much fun growing old together.


00:23:29.458 --> 00:23:32.359
Why don't you just have her perform
if you like her so much?


00:23:32.527 --> 00:23:34.791
Because, honey, look at you.


00:23:34.963 --> 00:23:37.090
You are a star.


00:23:37.265 --> 00:23:41.463
That is what Guy Morgan needs.
You, the star.


00:23:41.636 --> 00:23:43.194
I'm a star.


00:23:43.371 --> 00:23:47.535
- A bright, gassy star.
- Yes, you are.


00:23:47.709 --> 00:23:50.109
And Guy Morgan is gonna
give you a swimming pool...


00:23:50.278 --> 00:23:52.246
...shaped just like Colin Farrell.


00:23:52.414 --> 00:23:53.972
Every part of him.


00:23:54.149 --> 00:23:57.676
Or, Bev, you could just see every part
of Colin Farrell on the Internet.


00:23:57.853 --> 00:24:00.617
And just leave me out of this.


00:24:01.890 --> 00:24:04.450
- Okay, so how do we do this?
- First rule of Lie Club...


00:24:04.626 --> 00:24:06.526
...is don't talk about Lie Club.


00:24:07.129 --> 00:24:09.029
Which includes you, Katie.


00:24:09.197 --> 00:24:11.893
As far as everyone knows,
you can't sing.


00:24:12.067 --> 00:24:14.126
And no more talking to Luke or Guy.


00:24:14.302 --> 00:24:15.667
Are we clear?


00:24:16.104 --> 00:24:17.298
Crystal.


00:24:19.241 --> 00:24:22.233
Yeah, Dad, we're about to meet
some fresh talent right now.


00:24:22.410 --> 00:24:26.403
Remember when you signed Jay-Z?
No, you passed on him, my bad.


00:24:26.581 --> 00:24:29.049
Um, this is like that,
except it's gonna be brilliant.


00:24:29.217 --> 00:24:30.548
Yeah. Okay.


00:24:30.719 --> 00:24:32.846
- Yeah, okay. Bye.
- Dude, what'd he say?


00:24:33.021 --> 00:24:34.545
These guys you told me about are good?


00:24:34.723 --> 00:24:38.090
Yes. The Oral Majority has potential.
They'll be here any second.


00:24:38.260 --> 00:24:40.956
Talking about potential,
how was your little date with Bev?


00:24:41.129 --> 00:24:43.393
- Her mom kicked me out.
- I told you. Bev is drama.


00:24:43.565 --> 00:24:45.123
Technically, it was Gail's drama.


00:24:45.300 --> 00:24:47.427
But Bev's interesting, man. She's...


00:24:47.602 --> 00:24:49.069
I'm worried she's bonkers.


00:24:49.237 --> 00:24:52.070
See, my last girlfriend, she was hot,
but absolutely mental.


00:24:52.240 --> 00:24:54.902
I need a girl who's not gonna be
shipped to the loony bin.


00:24:55.076 --> 00:24:56.839
Hang on, I'm gonna hit the facilities.


00:24:57.012 --> 00:24:58.707
Facilities. That's a new one.


00:24:59.147 --> 00:25:01.843
- Hey, man. Sorry we're late.
- Hey, what's good, y'all?


00:25:02.017 --> 00:25:04.747
Nobody talks to my boy
until he comes from the facilities.


00:25:04.920 --> 00:25:06.114
We're here to impress.


00:25:06.288 --> 00:25:08.552
- Clear, right?
- Got it.


00:25:12.394 --> 00:25:14.862
<i>When you're fighting just to keep it sane</i>


00:25:15.030 --> 00:25:17.294
<i>Throw your will
At the eye of the hurricane</i>


00:25:17.465 --> 00:25:19.660
<i>- Sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:19.834 --> 00:25:23.201
<i>- Help me sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:23.371 --> 00:25:25.896
<i>If you wanna find out who you are
Stop running</i>


00:25:26.074 --> 00:25:29.339
<i>In the end you'll figure out
It's all about nothing</i>


00:25:29.511 --> 00:25:34.813
<i>All night, it's gonna be all right
Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>


00:25:34.983 --> 00:25:41.718
<i>All right
Turn your dreams into your life</i>


00:25:42.924 --> 00:25:44.414
That's good.


00:25:51.466 --> 00:25:54.765
I'm clean. No one followed me.
And I got your intel.


00:25:55.604 --> 00:25:57.936
Oh, Katie, baby, your life sucks.


00:25:58.106 --> 00:26:00.006
Trust me, it gets worse.


00:26:01.042 --> 00:26:04.637
Okay, dude, those guys, they
just went Oral Majority on me in there...


00:26:04.813 --> 00:26:07.008
- I was trying to hold them back...
- You're right.


00:26:07.182 --> 00:26:09.116
They have potential and they're great.


00:26:09.284 --> 00:26:14.517
But first, my talent-finding friend,
promise me no more auditions in the bogs.


00:26:14.689 --> 00:26:16.884
- The what?
- The loo.


00:26:17.425 --> 00:26:19.188
- Bathroom. Toilet.
- Got it.


00:26:19.361 --> 00:26:21.955
All right. Okay, come on.
I wanna show you something.


00:26:22.564 --> 00:26:25.863
So now I have to rehearse in secret.


00:26:26.034 --> 00:26:27.501
Why not not rehearse?


00:26:27.669 --> 00:26:29.694
Make Bev sound bad. What do you care?


00:26:29.871 --> 00:26:32.863
No song, no savings account. No life.


00:26:35.043 --> 00:26:37.477
People. Coming. Now.


00:26:41.016 --> 00:26:42.847
Okay.


00:26:43.418 --> 00:26:45.784
Dude, what are we doing?
The suspense is killing me.


00:26:46.121 --> 00:26:47.884
Can you grab the mike?


00:26:48.056 --> 00:26:50.047
Not about to serenade
a brother, are you?


00:26:50.225 --> 00:26:52.056
Dude, with bromance, comes a fine line.


00:26:52.227 --> 00:26:54.525
That I shall not cross.


00:26:54.996 --> 00:26:57.294
So sing something.


00:26:58.967 --> 00:27:00.434
Okay.


00:27:04.572 --> 00:27:07.370
<i>I'm lost in a world
That rattles my brain</i>


00:27:07.542 --> 00:27:10.033
<i>I'm cleaning up my life
From the mess you made</i>


00:27:10.211 --> 00:27:11.610
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:12.080 --> 00:27:14.071
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:15.884 --> 00:27:18.352
<i>My soul's in debt, but my bills are paid</i>


00:27:18.520 --> 00:27:21.045
<i>I'd give anything just to make an escape</i>


00:27:21.222 --> 00:27:22.814
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:23.325 --> 00:27:24.952
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:25.960 --> 00:27:28.895
<i>So you can keep
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:29.064 --> 00:27:31.396
<i>Baby, you're rockin'
But there ain't no way I'm ever letting you in</i>


00:27:31.566 --> 00:27:33.033
<i>He's amazing.</i>


00:27:34.436 --> 00:27:36.097
<i>Not again</i>


00:27:37.038 --> 00:27:39.871
<i>So keep on
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:40.041 --> 00:27:45.240
<i>But, baby, you're better off walking
'Cause I ain't gonna let you in</i>


00:27:45.413 --> 00:27:46.971
<i>Never again</i>


00:27:48.083 --> 00:27:50.677
<i>I went out on a limb again</i>


00:27:50.852 --> 00:27:53.412
<i>I guess I had to lose to win</i>


00:27:53.588 --> 00:27:57.957
<i>I was too confused to know
Which way to turn</i>


00:27:59.361 --> 00:28:02.023
<i>- And she could be a millionaire...
- Crap.</i>


00:28:02.197 --> 00:28:04.461
<i>- Gail needs me to drive her home.
- I don't care</i>


00:28:04.632 --> 00:28:07.294
<i>'Cause, baby, there's nobody home</i>


00:28:07.469 --> 00:28:09.960
<i>Nobody's home at all, yeah</i>


00:28:14.442 --> 00:28:16.569
- What? Did you write that?
- Yeah.


00:28:16.745 --> 00:28:19.373
Reminds me of, um... Uh...


00:28:19.547 --> 00:28:22.880
- Danger Fruit, right? Danger Fruit.
- Ha, ha. Because I wrote their album too.


00:28:23.151 --> 00:28:25.642
Shut up. Took me forever
to find that bootleg online.


00:28:25.820 --> 00:28:27.811
- I love that album. That's crazy.
- Yeah.


00:28:27.989 --> 00:28:30.287
My dad doesn't know.
And he thought the record...


00:28:30.458 --> 00:28:32.153
...was a pile of crap.


00:28:32.427 --> 00:28:34.122
He thinks writing's a waste of time.


00:28:34.562 --> 00:28:38.396
Because he basically wants me
to be like him. Only with better hair.


00:28:38.867 --> 00:28:42.963
But the first thing I thought when
I heard those guys in the urinals was...


00:28:43.138 --> 00:28:44.162
...good acoustics.


00:28:44.572 --> 00:28:48.406
Second thought was these guys,
these guys could be great.


00:28:48.576 --> 00:28:50.168
If you gave them your song.


00:28:51.579 --> 00:28:53.240
Mate, that's a brilliant idea.


00:28:53.982 --> 00:28:56.678
- So put them in the Showcase?
- Put them in the Showcase.


00:28:56.851 --> 00:28:58.182
Yeah.


00:28:59.854 --> 00:29:06.384
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:29:06.694 --> 00:29:07.991
You wrote that song today?


00:29:08.163 --> 00:29:11.621
- You've been home for what, two hours?
- It's like an answer to his song.


00:29:11.900 --> 00:29:13.197
You really like this guy.


00:29:13.368 --> 00:29:15.063
Yeah, I'm an idiot.


00:29:15.236 --> 00:29:17.431
You have to sing that for him.


00:29:17.605 --> 00:29:21.097
What if you sang to him in secret?


00:29:22.911 --> 00:29:25.709
At the dance. Ta-da.


00:29:29.317 --> 00:29:32.150
Okay, I know the card's
like, really cheesy, but...


00:29:34.189 --> 00:29:36.657
Oh, God, I hope you like it.


00:29:36.991 --> 00:29:40.483
Ange, it's beautiful,
but are you crazy?


00:29:40.662 --> 00:29:42.687
No, I know you're crazy.


00:29:42.864 --> 00:29:43.888
Am not.


00:29:44.933 --> 00:29:47.925
- What if he doesn't even like me?
- You'll both be in disguise.


00:29:48.102 --> 00:29:50.798
It's your chance to see
if he was really flirting with you.


00:29:50.972 --> 00:29:53.532
I was naked. Of course he was flirting.


00:29:53.708 --> 00:29:56.404
And why even torture myself?
It's not like I can have him.


00:29:56.578 --> 00:29:58.512
Why not? Tell him how you feel.


00:29:58.680 --> 00:30:02.707
If he feels the same way, you can reveal
your hot self and he won't tell Gail.


00:30:03.084 --> 00:30:06.178
And if he hates the song,
leave the disguise on.


00:30:09.123 --> 00:30:10.647
Okay.


00:30:10.959 --> 00:30:12.551
I'm going to the dance.


00:30:12.727 --> 00:30:14.058
That's my girl.


00:30:14.329 --> 00:30:18.322
<i>Maurice, no, no.
Again, in Français, longer legs.</i>


00:30:18.500 --> 00:30:21.799
I wouldn't go in your closet
for a little while if I were you.


00:30:21.970 --> 00:30:23.733
What? Why?


00:30:23.905 --> 00:30:25.270
Hey. Wake up.


00:30:29.177 --> 00:30:30.735
Katie!


00:30:30.912 --> 00:30:34.348
The cat has pooped in my closet.
I need you to clean it up.


00:30:34.516 --> 00:30:36.006
Go.


00:30:36.184 --> 00:30:37.913
I told you we don't have a cat.


00:30:38.086 --> 00:30:39.417
Angie, heads up.


00:30:41.389 --> 00:30:42.686
Katie!


00:30:47.896 --> 00:30:49.625
What's going on?


00:30:49.797 --> 00:30:51.230
Nothing.


00:30:51.399 --> 00:30:54.527
I am, uh, re-organizing and labeling. I...


00:30:54.702 --> 00:30:57.000
I took up crochet.
Do you want new socks?


00:30:57.171 --> 00:31:01.232
I would make you a sweater, but I hear
that the arms, that they're really hard.


00:31:04.479 --> 00:31:08.643
Oh, you thought you could sneak off
and go to the dance.


00:31:08.816 --> 00:31:11.046
After what you pulled today with Guy.


00:31:11.219 --> 00:31:12.652
Oh, no, no.


00:31:12.820 --> 00:31:15.311
Oh, no, no, no.


00:31:15.490 --> 00:31:17.788
You're on Victor watch tonight...


00:31:17.959 --> 00:31:20.655
...tomorrow night and every night.


00:31:20.828 --> 00:31:21.852
Fun.


00:31:22.030 --> 00:31:25.158
I'll give Victor all the mothering
you don't have time for.


00:31:25.333 --> 00:31:28.734
Oh, I wish you could be my mommy.


00:31:29.604 --> 00:31:31.629
I'm off to my cinnamon colonic.


00:31:35.610 --> 00:31:37.976
Hey. Get down.
You're gonna break yourself.


00:31:38.313 --> 00:31:40.577
Or worse, the furniture.


00:31:40.882 --> 00:31:43.976
Hello?
- Hey.


00:31:44.252 --> 00:31:47.415
- You look like you're having fun.
- Always.


00:31:47.755 --> 00:31:50.815
Well, I couldn't let you not go to the dance
without me.


00:31:50.992 --> 00:31:53.392
Besides, we have six hours
of shirtless Team Jacob.


00:31:53.561 --> 00:31:56.496
So let's just get this party started.


00:31:56.664 --> 00:32:00.691
- So is Victor driving you nuts?
- I swear to you, he's not human.


00:32:00.969 --> 00:32:04.268
I mean, can you really blame him, though?
Just look at this family.


00:32:05.473 --> 00:32:06.770
Victor, what are you doing?


00:32:16.751 --> 00:32:19.015
Oh, no. Great.


00:32:19.187 --> 00:32:21.382
Eh, she actually looks prettier
that way.


00:32:21.990 --> 00:32:25.016
True. Ugh. Whatever.


00:32:26.194 --> 00:32:29.322
Why did I ever think that tonight
could've been something special.


00:32:30.098 --> 00:32:32.362
Think Bev's all over Luke at the dance
right now?


00:32:32.533 --> 00:32:34.831
They're probably making out. See?


00:32:35.003 --> 00:32:38.200
- Victor, give it a rest.
- Just check it out. Come on.


00:32:41.409 --> 00:32:44.037
<i>Luke is gonna produce
whoever wins the Showcase.</i>


00:32:44.212 --> 00:32:47.272
<i>So we need a little insurance.</i>


00:32:47.448 --> 00:32:50.645
<i>- I know what I'm doing, Mother.
Do you?</i>


00:32:51.552 --> 00:32:54.419
I can't take it anymore, okay?


00:32:54.589 --> 00:32:56.648
I'm taking my life into my own hands.


00:32:56.824 --> 00:32:57.916
I'm talking to Luke.


00:32:58.526 --> 00:33:01.017
- Finally.
- Okay, but we have gotta be home...


00:33:01.195 --> 00:33:02.662
...before Gail gets here.


00:33:03.398 --> 00:33:04.729
What about the demon spawn?


00:33:04.899 --> 00:33:05.923
Mm-hm.


00:33:06.100 --> 00:33:07.499
Right.


00:33:08.503 --> 00:33:09.902
Okay, just watch him.


00:33:12.974 --> 00:33:14.236
Hmm.


00:33:19.047 --> 00:33:21.038
Is that all you've got, Angela?


00:33:21.716 --> 00:33:22.740
Ravi?


00:33:24.419 --> 00:33:26.944
My sister could catch that, jerknut.


00:33:27.121 --> 00:33:29.555
Put some nuts in that sack, ref.


00:33:31.693 --> 00:33:34.253
Miss Katie, I am most startled.


00:33:34.429 --> 00:33:35.623
Obviously.


00:33:36.164 --> 00:33:38.655
All right. All right. Don't hate me.


00:33:38.833 --> 00:33:40.391
Okay, don't hate me. I'm sorry.


00:33:40.568 --> 00:33:43.935
But my name ain't Ravi. It's Tony.


00:33:44.472 --> 00:33:47.600
- Tony.
- Tony Gupta from Jersey.


00:33:47.775 --> 00:33:50.437
- From Jersey.
- I am half Indian.


00:33:50.812 --> 00:33:54.213
My friends call me Meatball
because I'm half Italian.


00:33:54.382 --> 00:33:56.247
Truth is I always wanted to be an actor.


00:33:56.617 --> 00:33:58.141
But I never got my shot.


00:33:58.319 --> 00:34:00.549
I'm working at KFC,
and one day, Gail comes in...


00:34:00.722 --> 00:34:03.122
...she's like, "Are you Indian?"
I'm like, "What?"


00:34:03.291 --> 00:34:05.486
She's like, "Are you a guru?"
I'm like:


00:34:05.660 --> 00:34:07.150
"Who is asking?"


00:34:07.428 --> 00:34:10.795
She says, "Someone
who's paying for some spiritual guidance."


00:34:10.965 --> 00:34:13.559
And I'm like, "Whaa! It's a miracle!"


00:34:13.735 --> 00:34:18.104
I finally get a chance to do
a total immersion into a character.


00:34:18.406 --> 00:34:20.670
Real training and I get paid.
Are you kidding me?


00:34:20.842 --> 00:34:23.242
Ravi is my King Lear.


00:34:23.578 --> 00:34:26.206
<i>You wanna hear
the monologue from My Fair Lady?</i>


00:34:26.380 --> 00:34:27.574
- Oy, mate.
- No, thanks.


00:34:28.783 --> 00:34:31.479
I'm sorry I barged in. Whoops.


00:34:34.288 --> 00:34:37.951
Your secret's safe with me, okay?
But I need to ask you a favor.


00:34:38.626 --> 00:34:40.685
- Meatball.
- Ha, Meatball.


00:34:40.862 --> 00:34:43.330
Please watch Victor tonight
so I can go to the dance?


00:34:43.498 --> 00:34:44.556
Are you kidding me? Done.


00:34:46.134 --> 00:34:47.465
Blow it up.


00:34:49.403 --> 00:34:50.961
Thank you.


00:35:00.782 --> 00:35:02.181
Whoa.


00:35:02.350 --> 00:35:04.978
How am I supposed to find Luke
if everybody's got a mask?


00:35:05.153 --> 00:35:08.213
I never said this was
gonna be easy. Let's do some recon.


00:35:09.590 --> 00:35:11.922
I am Assistant Principal
Dorothy Plumberg.


00:35:12.093 --> 00:35:15.324
No drinking. No texting. No kissing.


00:35:18.032 --> 00:35:21.001
Luke? No. Luke Morgan?


00:35:21.169 --> 00:35:24.798
No leaving the premises
and no experiencing joy of any kind.


00:35:25.506 --> 00:35:27.838
Luke? Ugh.


00:35:33.214 --> 00:35:34.647
Where is he?


00:35:35.483 --> 00:35:38.281
That reminds me.
I got a new act for you to listen to.


00:35:38.452 --> 00:35:40.113
- Now?
- No time like it.


00:35:40.288 --> 00:35:42.722
- Dude, not again...
- We're called Big Pain Ticket.


00:35:46.227 --> 00:35:49.788
<i>I wanna kiss your apocalypse</i>


00:35:49.964 --> 00:35:53.297
<i>Wrap you in my Armageddon</i>


00:35:53.467 --> 00:35:55.662
<i>Sing you a twisted serenade</i>


00:35:55.870 --> 00:35:58.600
They're good, but I'm worried
that chain saw's unsafe.


00:35:58.773 --> 00:36:01.207
Dude, the chain saw's,
like, the best part.


00:36:08.015 --> 00:36:09.073
I think I found him.


00:36:09.250 --> 00:36:11.514
Well, he is blond.


00:36:14.622 --> 00:36:16.920
Oh, my God, what is she doing here?


00:36:18.826 --> 00:36:21.124
I hate teenage desperation.


00:36:21.295 --> 00:36:22.694
What are you doing here?


00:36:22.864 --> 00:36:25.697
Oh, honey, the prize pig
doesn't win the blue ribbon...


00:36:25.867 --> 00:36:27.892
...by covering up its third best asset.


00:36:28.069 --> 00:36:31.004
A, what does that even mean
and, B, did you just call me a pig?


00:36:31.172 --> 00:36:33.003
Honey, I saw you making sweet love...


00:36:33.174 --> 00:36:35.642
...to a plate of Swedish meatballs
at the snack table.


00:36:38.079 --> 00:36:40.206
It's now or never, babe.


00:36:41.749 --> 00:36:45.185
- What if she recognizes me?
- I'll distract her. Go.


00:36:45.353 --> 00:36:47.548
- So was I right or was I right?
- You were right.


00:36:47.722 --> 00:36:50.589
You have very cool taste.
Any more auditions in the men's...


00:36:50.758 --> 00:36:52.692
...and you're fired.


00:36:55.730 --> 00:36:59.257
- I know your secret.
- Which secret is that?


00:37:01.869 --> 00:37:03.359
I heard you sing at school.


00:37:03.604 --> 00:37:04.730
You were amazing.


00:37:04.906 --> 00:37:05.964
Do I know you?


00:37:10.311 --> 00:37:12.905
- I wanna show you something.
- What's your name?


00:37:15.249 --> 00:37:17.308
Angela, what are you doing?


00:37:17.952 --> 00:37:20.443
I'd like to make a request.


00:37:24.959 --> 00:37:27.792
I will make your night. I promise.


00:37:27.962 --> 00:37:29.327
Miss Van R.


00:37:29.964 --> 00:37:32.364
Is it true you wanted to be a dancer
when you were younger...


00:37:32.533 --> 00:37:33.727
...but were never good enough?


00:37:35.102 --> 00:37:36.763
Who told you that?


00:37:54.488 --> 00:37:55.921
Well, now, how lovely.


00:37:56.090 --> 00:37:59.287
But I've seen better dancing
in a Filipino prison, sugar.


00:37:59.460 --> 00:38:00.586
Oh!


00:38:00.761 --> 00:38:04.993
Really? Because I think
I just challenged you to a dance battle.


00:38:09.337 --> 00:38:12.431
Would Luke Morgan please pick up
the white courtesy phone?


00:38:12.606 --> 00:38:15.507
Luke Morgan, white courtesy phone.


00:38:20.281 --> 00:38:23.011
Hold on. What is that?
You've never seen a guitar before?


00:38:23.351 --> 00:38:26.047
You hid a guitar in there.
You hiding anything else?


00:38:26.220 --> 00:38:27.482
Follow me.


00:38:32.526 --> 00:38:34.357
Oh, wow.


00:38:36.831 --> 00:38:42.394
Madam, while your exquisite eyes
tell of a radiant, but mischievous beauty...


00:38:43.270 --> 00:38:45.170
...I have grown impatient.


00:38:45.339 --> 00:38:49.036
Off with your veil,
so that I may know the truth.


00:38:50.544 --> 00:38:51.738
Or not.


00:38:54.015 --> 00:38:57.041
I'm hoping this answers
a lot of your questions.


00:39:03.257 --> 00:39:06.818
<i>I can see it from the spark in your eyes</i>


00:39:08.129 --> 00:39:12.361
<i>You believe in all the things
You've denied</i>


00:39:12.533 --> 00:39:16.060
<i>You wanna fly
And leave your worries behind</i>


00:39:16.237 --> 00:39:20.230
<i>Don't you? Don't you?</i>


00:39:22.209 --> 00:39:25.542
<i>Well, now I'm knocking
At your front door</i>


00:39:27.314 --> 00:39:31.011
<i>And I'm looking for the right cure</i>


00:39:31.685 --> 00:39:35.382
<i>I'm still a little bit unsure</i>


00:39:35.856 --> 00:39:38.689
Okay, now take off that veil.


00:39:39.160 --> 00:39:40.252
Uh-uh.


00:42:19.186 --> 00:42:21.780
I think I've blown something.


00:42:21.956 --> 00:42:25.016
Does anyone else smell cinnamon?


00:42:27.628 --> 00:42:29.186
Move it, fatso.


00:42:30.931 --> 00:42:37.530
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:42:38.272 --> 00:42:41.901
Okay, you are blowing my mind.
You have to show me who you are.


00:42:54.455 --> 00:42:55.888
- We have to go.
- What?


00:42:56.056 --> 00:42:58.081
- Come.
- No, Ange.


00:42:58.259 --> 00:43:00.819
In the middle of a really big moment
right now.


00:43:00.995 --> 00:43:02.963
Someone had an accident
and went home.


00:43:05.432 --> 00:43:06.797
I'm so sorry.


00:43:07.501 --> 00:43:08.729
What...? You...?


00:43:09.436 --> 00:43:11.097
Hey. Wait.


00:43:11.272 --> 00:43:12.500
But who are you?


00:43:12.673 --> 00:43:15.267
Over here. Go, go, go.


00:43:23.417 --> 00:43:26.443
- We beat her.
- I love you for this.


00:43:44.905 --> 00:43:46.930
Interesting babysitting attire.


00:43:47.708 --> 00:43:50.643
I should've known
you'd go behind my back again.


00:43:51.078 --> 00:43:54.013
And that Paula Abdul wannabe,
trying to distract me.


00:43:54.348 --> 00:43:56.543
Don't talk about her like that.


00:43:58.552 --> 00:44:01.715
Your friend wants to be a choreographer,
if memory serves.


00:44:01.889 --> 00:44:05.450
She might've made a decent one
if she hadn't gotten herself expelled.


00:44:05.626 --> 00:44:07.890
Guess she can kiss
them Juilliard dreams goodbye.


00:44:08.062 --> 00:44:11.122
Look, I'll do whatever you want.
Okay? Just leave Ange out of this.


00:44:11.432 --> 00:44:14.560
That depends if you pull another stunt
like tonight, sugar.


00:44:15.469 --> 00:44:18.597
- I won't.
- I'll be taking this.


00:44:25.112 --> 00:44:28.343
Only her eyes were piercing out
through this veil, but her voice...


00:44:28.515 --> 00:44:30.574
How hot was the girl
on a scale of one to 10?


00:44:30.751 --> 00:44:32.685
- An 11.
- The hotness scale only goes 10.


00:44:32.853 --> 00:44:34.548
Yeah, this girl has love potential.


00:44:34.722 --> 00:44:37.020
- Ooh, love.
- Shut it.


00:44:38.392 --> 00:44:42.522
We are gonna do this for hours
until we get it right. Even if it takes hours.


00:44:43.497 --> 00:44:47.092
Now, sing like your life depends on it.
Because, sugar, it does.


00:44:48.168 --> 00:44:49.795
We're recording.


00:44:50.104 --> 00:44:51.935
<i>Plug in the mike</i>


00:44:52.106 --> 00:44:53.334
<i>Open the curtain</i>


00:44:53.941 --> 00:44:55.875
<i>Turn on the lights</i>


00:44:56.043 --> 00:44:57.772
<i>I'm through rehearsing</i>


00:44:57.945 --> 00:45:00.277
- Dang, she's good, man.
- Told you, man.


00:45:00.447 --> 00:45:01.675
Check this out, all right?


00:45:01.849 --> 00:45:05.444
Thirty-nine girls in the singing program
which means 85 percent...


00:45:05.619 --> 00:45:07.450
...have music during the sixth period.


00:45:07.621 --> 00:45:09.452
So your girl's in one of those rooms.


00:45:09.656 --> 00:45:11.681
<i>The feeling ignites</i>


00:45:11.859 --> 00:45:13.019
<i>I'm in control</i>


00:45:13.193 --> 00:45:15.161
Oh, cut. Cut.


00:45:15.329 --> 00:45:17.194
That was subpar at best.


00:45:17.364 --> 00:45:19.889
From the top, pretty please.


00:45:20.634 --> 00:45:23.933
<i>Amazing grace</i>


00:45:24.104 --> 00:45:25.662
It's cool, I got this.


00:45:25.839 --> 00:45:28.205
Ladies, all my single ladies.


00:45:28.375 --> 00:45:31.401
My boy Luke here has a special favor
to ask of you, all right?


00:45:31.578 --> 00:45:34.672
He needs vocals
for this big show coming up, so...


00:45:34.848 --> 00:45:36.406
- My name is...
- Luke Morgan.


00:45:36.850 --> 00:45:39.717
You will put me in the Showcase.
Oh, yes, you will.


00:45:40.254 --> 00:45:43.815
- Maybe I could ask you to sing first?
- I am so gonna rock your world.


00:45:44.091 --> 00:45:47.424
<i>I love the way you love me, Luke</i>


00:45:47.594 --> 00:45:50.188
<i>Inside my head every night</i>


00:45:50.364 --> 00:45:52.832
<i>You come and kiss me good night</i>


00:45:53.000 --> 00:45:56.094
<i>Whatever you see is what you get</i>


00:45:56.270 --> 00:45:58.795
Why don't you not suck
and do it again, okay?


00:46:00.541 --> 00:46:05.137
<i>I wanna be with you forever...</i>


00:46:05.312 --> 00:46:08.281
What is going on in here? Disgusting.


00:46:08.449 --> 00:46:11.282
You two boys are not in my class.
Stop. Wait.


00:46:17.324 --> 00:46:20.521
Stop. Wait. Stop.


00:46:39.646 --> 00:46:41.944
<i>I got nothing to lose</i>


00:46:42.115 --> 00:46:43.309
<i>I've been exposed</i>


00:46:43.484 --> 00:46:45.782
<i>I'm paying my dues</i>


00:46:45.953 --> 00:46:47.318
<i>Playing the role</i>


00:46:48.155 --> 00:46:50.282
- Oh, really?
- We are back where we started.


00:46:50.457 --> 00:46:51.583
This is not good.


00:46:53.160 --> 00:46:54.957
That's her. That's her voice.


00:46:55.128 --> 00:46:56.959
Don't think you can get away from me.


00:46:57.130 --> 00:46:59.530
- Step aside. Step aside.
- Please. Wait.


00:46:59.700 --> 00:47:03.136
Okay. But first, why don't you
just both audition for me.


00:47:03.303 --> 00:47:04.327
Listen...


00:47:04.505 --> 00:47:07.941
<i>Luke, you are the one for me, yes you are</i>


00:47:08.108 --> 00:47:09.769
<i>You just don't know it yet</i>


00:47:21.622 --> 00:47:25.615
<i>Make you believe in me</i>


00:47:25.792 --> 00:47:28.784
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:28.962 --> 00:47:32.591
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:32.766 --> 00:47:36.702
<i>That I can be
Anything, anything, anything</i>


00:47:36.870 --> 00:47:40.670
<i>I'll make you believe in me</i>


00:47:41.208 --> 00:47:44.109
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:44.278 --> 00:47:47.338
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:49.149 --> 00:47:51.083
It was you?


00:47:51.752 --> 00:47:54.846
- Oh, sorry to interrupt.
- Oh, no, honey. Interrupt away.


00:47:55.789 --> 00:47:59.623
I didn't think I'd see you. It was killing me.
Because I felt like we connected.


00:48:01.261 --> 00:48:04.287
Excuse me.
Uh, how exactly did you two connect?


00:48:04.464 --> 00:48:07.228
Yeah, how did we? I mean, we did.


00:48:07.401 --> 00:48:09.528
- Through...
- With your lyrics. They just...


00:48:10.170 --> 00:48:12.900
- I can't get them out of my head.
- My lyrics. Yeah.


00:48:13.173 --> 00:48:14.936
Well, how wonderful.


00:48:15.108 --> 00:48:18.475
But, uh, Bev has to prepare
for her Showcase audition.


00:48:18.645 --> 00:48:20.909
Oh, no. She doesn't need to audition.
You're in.


00:48:22.416 --> 00:48:24.213
Do you wanna grab a bite later?


00:48:24.384 --> 00:48:25.476
- Yeah.
Wait.


00:48:26.420 --> 00:48:27.887
You have a date with detention.


00:48:28.055 --> 00:48:29.522
Actually, he has a date with me.


00:48:29.690 --> 00:48:31.419
Dear me, did I not fire you?


00:48:31.592 --> 00:48:34.288
- I have tenure.
- One call and you're wearing a paper hat...


00:48:34.461 --> 00:48:37.589
...that says "Welcome to McDonald's.
How may I take your order?"


00:48:37.764 --> 00:48:39.254
- Five calls.
- Two calls and text.


00:48:39.433 --> 00:48:41.333
Two calls, a text, several long e-mails.


00:48:41.501 --> 00:48:44.299
One text and a Tweet.
- One text and a re-Tweet.


00:48:44.471 --> 00:48:46.837
Oh, for God's sakes,
go lick a chalkboard.


00:48:47.007 --> 00:48:48.474
Fine.


00:48:49.276 --> 00:48:50.800
I hate you.


00:48:54.448 --> 00:48:58.578
Okay. Um, I'd love to write a song with you.
Let's talk about it tonight?


00:48:58.852 --> 00:49:00.786
- I'd love to.
- Okay, you're on.


00:49:07.361 --> 00:49:08.988
I've always wanted to write a song.


00:49:09.162 --> 00:49:12.359
Maybe I'll write about my skin.
They say love tightens your pores.


00:49:12.532 --> 00:49:13.999
What rhymes with pores?


00:49:14.167 --> 00:49:16.965
Chores. Bores. Sores.


00:49:17.137 --> 00:49:19.332
Katie, I've got a new task for you.


